    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d109">

                <pb facs="0343" n="331" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg331"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by Colonel J. W. Middleton to Lieutenant
                        General Alvan C. Gillem, Jr.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chungking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-01">1 April 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The approved directive to Executive Headquarters contains a statement that each
                    organization to be retained in the Chinese Army will institute a twelve (12)
                    weeks’ basic training program. It is believed that such a program can best be
                    prepared by the group now in Nanking under General McClure.<anchor n="47"
                        xml:id="d109-f1"/> It is suggested the following radio be transmitted:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“To: Commanding General, Nanking Headquarters Command.</p>
                        <p>Request you prepare a 12 weeks’ basic training program for units of
                            Chinese Army to be retained after demobilization. This program is <pb
                                facs="0344" n="332" xml:id="pg332"/> for interim training to keep
                            troops occupied during period in which they have nothing else to do and
                            must be capable of being operated entirely by Chinese. Request such a
                            program be delivered to Chungking in one week. Colonel McClure,<anchor
                                n="48" xml:id="d109-f2"/> of your headquarters, is familiar with the
                            requirements.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right">Signed, Gillem.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed>J. W. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Middleton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d109-f1" n="47" xml:id="d109-f1-content">
                <p>Maj. Gen. Robert B. McClure, acting head of the Military Advisory Group being
                    organized at Nanking.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d109-f2" n="48" xml:id="d109-f2-content">
                <p>Col. Clinton I. McClure, U. S. A.</p>
            </note>
